# API Conventions

## CRUD resource pattern
Every new resource (e.g. `CustomerSla`, `AllowedImage`) follows this layout:

**`api/app/models.py`** — SQLAlchemy model
```python
class MyResource(Base):
    __tablename__ = "my_resources"
    id: Mapped[uuid.UUID] = mapped_column(UUID(as_uuid=True), primary_key=True, default=uuid.uuid4)
    name: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(512), unique=True)
    created_at: Mapped[dt.datetime] = mapped_column(DateTime(timezone=True), default=lambda: dt.datetime.now(dt.UTC))
    updated_at: Mapped[dt.datetime] = mapped_column(DateTime(timezone=True), default=..., onupdate=...)
```

**`api/app/main.py`** — four routes + Pydantic models + serializer
```python
class MyResourceCreateIn(BaseModel):
    name: str

class MyResourceUpdateIn(BaseModel):
    name: str | None = None

def _my_resource_to_api(row: MyResource) -> dict:
    return {"id": str(row.id), "name": row.name, ...}

@app.get("/api/my-resources")
def list_my_resources(db: Session = Depends(get_db)): ...

@app.post("/api/my-resources", status_code=201)
def create_my_resource(payload: MyResourceCreateIn, db: Session = Depends(get_db)): ...

@app.put("/api/my-resources/{resource_id}")
def update_my_resource(resource_id: uuid.UUID, payload: MyResourceUpdateIn, db: Session = Depends(get_db)): ...

@app.delete("/api/my-resources/{resource_id}", status_code=204)
def delete_my_resource(resource_id: uuid.UUID, db: Session = Depends(get_db)): ...
```

Helpers with non-trivial logic (normalization, lookup sets) live in a **separate module** (e.g. `api/app/allowed_images.py`), not inside `main.py`.

## Health probe convention
`_probe_<component>()` functions always return `{"status": "ok" | "error", "host": "<host:port>"}`:
```python
def _probe_postgres() -> dict:
    host = _pg_host()  # parsed from settings.postgres_dsn
    try:
        with engine.connect() as conn:
            conn.execute(text("SELECT 1"))
        return {"status": "ok", "host": host}
    except Exception as exc:
        return {"status": "error", "host": host, "detail": str(exc)[:200]}
```

## Settings
Add new config to `api/app/config.py` as a typed Pydantic field with a sensible default. Never read `os.environ` directly in route handlers.

## Error handling
Use `raise HTTPException(status_code=..., detail="...")` — never return bare dicts for errors.
